# Around — environment variables
#
# Everything runs with NO configuration using an in-memory, seeded store
# (great for local dev and demos; state resets when the server restarts).
#
# For a real multi-device experiment (multiple phones seeing each other, data
# that survives restarts and works across serverless instances), point it at a
# Supabase / Postgres project:
#   1. Create a Supabase project.
#   2. Run supabase/schema.sql in the Supabase SQL editor.
#   3. Set the two variables below and redeploy.
#
# SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# Optional: password-protect the research dashboard (/admin/<venue>) and the
# reset action. When unset, the dashboard is open (fine for local dev). Set this
# to any strong secret before putting the app on a public URL.
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=choose-a-strong-password
